WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
[Cancer Among Veterans, Early Diagnosis]

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:26.000
[Presented by The Administrator of Veterans'
Affairs.]

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:39.000
[Produced by Division of Motion Pictures,
Department of the Interior.]

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:46.000
[Under the direction of Veterans Administration
Exhibits Committee. Photomicrography by 

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:59.000
L. H. Prince, M. D., Hines, Illinois. Photography
by Walter K. Scott.]

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:10.000
[Narrative by... Max Cutler, M. D., Consultant,
Tumor Clinic,

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:19.900
Veterans Administration Facility, Hines, Illinois.]

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:23.840
[Narrator:] Under the direction of the Administrator
of Veterans' Affairs, the Veterans Administration

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:29.020
is making every effort towards furnishing
ex-servicemen with the benefits of early diagnosis

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:32.300
and the prompt and skillful treatment of cancer.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:37.700
This parent hospital at Hines, Illinois provides
more than 400 beds for tumor cases and serves

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:42.080
as a training ground for physicians selected
to specialize in the diagnosis and treatment

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.020
of this disease.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:48.040
Leaving the beautiful and spacious grounds,
we enter the hospital where the Tumor Board

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:53.400
is in session and hear the voice of Dr. Max
Cutler, consultant in tumors at the Hines

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:58.660
facility, who will present his subject, the
early diagnosis of cancer. Dr. Cutler.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:05.660
[Dr. Max Cutler:] Early diagnosis is the keystone
to cancer control. An accurate diagnosis is

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:10.800
the basis of correct and effective treatment.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:16.470
All the progress that has been realized in
the surgical and radiation treatment of cancer

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:22.920
is of no avail unless the lesion is recognized
early and treated correctly before it has

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:23.880
become disseminated.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:30.880
[Dr. Max Cutler:] Thus early diagnosis resulting
in the elimination of precancerous conditions

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:38.470
and in the cure of early cancer is by far
the most important single factor in the curability

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:39.310
of this disease.

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:46.310
The external cancers can be detected in their
very early stages and are both presentable

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:54.100
and curable. The internal cancers unfortunately
present a much more complex problem.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:03:01.190
And although much can be accomplished by careful
attention to early diagnosis, real progress

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:08.190
in this group awaits the discovery of a diagnostic
test much more delicate then is now available.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:14.500
We will now consider three forms of cancer
which pass through definite precancerous stages

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:17.830
and are, therefore, not only curable but preventable.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:24.830
Cancer of the mouth, preceded by leukoplakia;
cancer of the skin preceded by hyperkeratosis;

00:03:25.489 --> 00:03:30.230
and melanoma preceded by apparently innocent
moles.

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:36.560
We begin with leukoplakia, one of our most
important precancerous conditions. This lesion

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:42.700
is ten times as common in men as in women.
Hence, 90 percent of cancers of the mouth

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:44.319
occur in men.

00:03:44.319 --> 00:03:50.800
The well known relation between tobacco and
leukoplakia has given rise to the term, "Smoker's

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:51.560
patch."

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:57.590
Here you see a leukoplakia of the mucous membrane
of the cheek in which smoking is the etiological

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:04.590
factor. An underlying susceptibility of the
tissues to nicotine must be present for leukoplakia

00:04:05.099 --> 00:04:06.569
to develop.

00:04:06.569 --> 00:04:13.069
In susceptible individuals, it is probable
that infinitesimal amounts of the stimulating

00:04:13.069 --> 00:04:17.709
chemical agent can result in this condition.

00:04:17.709 --> 00:04:24.300
The relationship between leukoplakia and cancer
is well-illustrated in this case, where you

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:31.300
see an intense radiation reaction after treatment
of a cancer of the right cheek, which developed

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.820
in a patch of leukoplakia.

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:40.820
Leukoplakia often occurs at the site of artificial
dentures as in this case. Here we see a diffuse

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:47.820
leukoplakia of the roof of the mouth in a
patient whose mucous membrane is evidently

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:52.289
susceptible to chronic irritation and to nicotine.

00:04:52.289 --> 00:04:59.289
A combination of factors is usually responsible
for this type of lesion. When a patch of leukoplakia

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:04.750
begins to undergo malignant degeneration,
it exhibits certain clinical signs.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:10.740
It becomes thickened and somewhat indurated
and its surface becomes fissured and eroded.

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:15.960
In this stage the lesion is either precancerous
or already fully malignant.

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:22.520
True ulceration almost invariably means that
carcinoma has become established. When these

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:29.490
clinical signs appear, a biopsy is usually
necessary to establish the diagnosis of cancer.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:35.099
In this connection it should be emphasized
that a negative biopsy by no means excludes

00:05:35.099 --> 00:05:40.470
the presence of cancer and one must be guided
largely by the clinical picture.

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:46.550
Dental caries is etiologically related to
cancer of the oral mucous membrane. A sharp

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:52.810
or broken tooth can produce repeated trauma
to the adjacent mucous membrane and results

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:55.860
in a traumatic ulcer and finally in carcinoma.

00:05:55.860 --> 00:06:02.150
This is a remarkable example of this type.
Note the precise relationship between this

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:07.500
jagged tooth and the lesion in the mucous
membrane of the cheek. Removal of the source

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:13.180
of irritation results in prompt disappearance
of the ulcer when it is only inflammatory.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:20.180
Leukoplakia of the oral mucous membrane frequently
arises at the site of dissimilar metal fillings

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:26.639
in patients who are non-smokers and in the
absence of both non-specific inflammation

00:06:26.639 --> 00:06:28.160
and syphilis.

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:33.240
The development of the leukoplakia at the
exact site of the dissimilar filling as in

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:39.180
this case and the absence of other etiologic
factors constitute significant evidence of

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:41.280
this probable relationship.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:46.770
The lateral border of the tongue being in
close proximity to carious and infected teeth

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:52.250
is a common site of leukoplakia. The dorsum
is affected more commonly when the lesion

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:55.320
is diffuse. Often it is on a syphilitic basis.

00:06:55.320 --> 00:07:02.070
Extensive diffuse leukoplakia is usually associated
with syphilis. The cancers of the lip and

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:08.360
tongue are quite independent. Each arose in
a separate patch of leukoplakia. Such lesions

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:13.479
may arise simultaneously or they may be separated
by months or years.

00:07:13.479 --> 00:07:20.280
The prognosis of cancer of the mouth associated
with syphilitic leukoplakia is extremely grave.

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:24.870
The modification in the connective tissue
and blood vessels resulting from the syphilitic

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:30.740
infection has a most unfavorable influence
upon the surgical and radiation result and

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:35.740
a cure is almost never accomplished in spite
of the efficiency and thoroughness of the

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:37.479
treatment.

00:07:37.479 --> 00:07:42.530
In spite of the early signs they produce,
cancers of the oral cavity still reach an

00:07:42.530 --> 00:07:48.949
advanced stage in many patients. The last
two cases are examples of this fact.

00:07:48.949 --> 00:07:55.840
Cancer of the lower lip is overwhelmingly
a disease of men. The lesion begins as a small

00:07:55.840 --> 00:08:00.880
localized nodularity which has to be differentiated
from a benign hyperkeratosis.

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:07.880
Lesions of this extent are readily curable
by surgery or by irradiation. In later stages

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:15.319
the disease spreads to the adjacent skin and
oral mucosa. And the lesion becomes indurated,

00:08:15.319 --> 00:08:17.410
ulcerated and painful as in this example.

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:22.990
Lesions of this extent are usually accompanied
by cervical adenopathy and when the growth

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:29.240
approaches or crosses the midline, one must
assume that the adenopathy is bilateral, even

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:32.319
though this is not demonstrable clinically.

00:08:32.319 --> 00:08:37.839
A projecting tooth, especially when it is
sharp, sometimes traumatizes the lip causing

00:08:37.839 --> 00:08:44.579
first an ulcer than a carcinoma. This is a
clinical example. Note the precise anatomical

00:08:44.579 --> 00:08:47.890
relation between the tooth and the carcinoma.

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:54.490
[ Showing lesion on lip ]

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:59.680
Cancer can begin in the mucous membrane of
the upper or lower lip or cheek as a small,

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:06.640
firm, circumscribed and movable tumor, which
grows slowly and remains non-ulcerated for

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:08.540
a long time.

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:13.930
These lesions originate in the epithelium
of ducts of mucous glands. Because they are

00:09:13.930 --> 00:09:20.709
non-ulcerated and freely movable they resemble
simple benign mucous cysts and are invariably

00:09:20.709 --> 00:09:22.260
so diagnosed.

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:28.630
They are usually removed inadequately and
recur promptly. They are often highly malignant

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:34.870
and unless this peculiar type of carcinoma
is diagnosed properly and treated correctly

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:37.270
the first time, the results are disastrous.

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:44.270
The 
differential diagnosis of cancer of the mouth
must consider benign papillomatous lesions,

00:09:52.589 --> 00:09:59.589
primary and tertiary syphilis, papilloma durum
of the tongue, tuberculosis and mixed tumors

00:09:59.959 --> 00:10:02.030
of salivary glands.

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:08.670
Here we have two cases of tuberculosis of
the mouth. Tuberculosis of the tongue is rare.

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:15.670
When it occurs, it is usually associated with
an active pulmonary lesion. Tuberculous ulcerations

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:22.120
appears as a flat non-indurated lesion which
is painful and tender.

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:28.550
The ulcer lacks the surrounding infiltration
and induration which is so characteristic

00:10:28.550 --> 00:10:34.920
of carcinoma. When the nature of the lesion
is in doubt clinically a biopsy should be

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:40.350
performed to establish the diagnosis with
certainty.

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:46.400
The aberrant salivary glands give rise to
an interesting and peculiar group of tumors.

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:51.439
In the mouth these tumors arise within the
cheek, the lip, the base of the tongue and

00:10:51.439 --> 00:10:57.490
the soft palate. Salivary glands and tumors
of the soft palate may reach a large size

00:10:57.490 --> 00:10:59.380
as seen in this case.

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:06.000
The small tumors are generally cured by wide
surgical removal. Inadequate excision is followed

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:11.829
by prompt recurrence. When these tumors reach
a large size and recur in older individuals,

00:11:11.829 --> 00:11:17.540
the patient's comfort and life expectancy
are often benefited by a conservative course.

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:22.970
The chief points in the differential diagnosis
are their location, their slow growth, and

00:11:22.970 --> 00:11:28.250
the fact that they remain circumscribed for
long periods. Unlike the carcinomas, they

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:33.130
remain non-ulcerated for many years in spite
of their large size.

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:38.500
There are three main types of skin cancer.
This is the basal cell form and it's commonly

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:44.170
referred to as "rodent ulcer." The next is
the squamous cell type with [inaudible] and

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:45.260
pearl formation.

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:51.089
And the third is the adenoid cystic type,
which is usually classified as a sub-variety

00:11:51.089 --> 00:11:58.089
of basal cell cancer. The majority of cancers
of the skin appear on the face.

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:05.870
Adenoid cystic carcinoma of the skin is a
form of basal cell cancer. This type is often

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:10.819
multiple and commonly affects the eyelids,
forehead and nose.

00:12:10.819 --> 00:12:17.010
The lesions are first elevated, then ulcerated.
As a rule they are more radio-resistant than

00:12:17.010 --> 00:12:20.189
the typical basal cell carcinomas.

00:12:20.189 --> 00:12:26.850
The nose is a common site of cancer of the
skin. The majority of the basal cell type,

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:33.209
regional metastasis generally does not occur
until the lesion has involved the mucous membrane.

00:12:33.209 --> 00:12:39.209
A great effort should be made to cure these
skin lesions at the first attempt, for each

00:12:39.209 --> 00:12:46.209
recurrence presents greater difficulty. The
first therapeutic procedure, be it surgery

00:12:46.329 --> 00:12:50.980
or irradiation, generally seals the patient's
fate.

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:57.980
The crucial importance of eradicating the
disease the first time can hardly be exaggerated.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:04.589
Advanced lesions such as these can be avoided
only by early diagnosis and thorough treatment

00:13:04.589 --> 00:13:08.199
when the patient first comes under observation.

00:13:08.199 --> 00:13:14.420
Here is a basal cell carcinoma of the lower
eyelid. The lesion is early and easily curable.

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:19.990
A surface application of radium administered
under correct conditions results in almost

00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:25.699
certain cure. But those must be the maximum
which the normal tissues will tolerate.

00:13:25.699 --> 00:13:30.230
Here is a basal cell carcinoma of the nose,
which has been treated and is beginning to

00:13:30.230 --> 00:13:35.360
undergo repair. Note that the edges of the
lesion have disappeared.

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:41.059
Seventy-five percent of cancers of the eyelid
are of the basal cell type. Regional lymph

00:13:41.059 --> 00:13:46.189
node metastasis occurs in 20 percent. The
inner [inaudible] of the lower eyelid is the

00:13:46.189 --> 00:13:48.069
most common site.

00:13:48.069 --> 00:13:54.709
In this case a carcinoma of the left lower
eyelid has disappeared after irradiation.

00:13:54.709 --> 00:14:01.309
But the sterilization was incomplete and several
years later an extension of the disease developed.

00:14:01.309 --> 00:14:07.990
Adequate irradiation as a rule avoids this
complication.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:13.439
Here we see one of the great tragedies of
this disease. How long did this patient wait

00:14:13.439 --> 00:14:15.209
before consulting his physician?

00:14:15.209 --> 00:14:21.069
Did the physician choose the best method of
treatment? How accurately and skillfully was

00:14:21.069 --> 00:14:21.600
the treatment executed?

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:28.600
These are the searching questions we as physicians
must constantly keep before us. Carcinomas

00:14:29.959 --> 00:14:36.199
of the scalp grow very slowly and almost never
invade the regional lymph nodes.

00:14:36.199 --> 00:14:43.199
They tend to adhere to the underlying bone
and are usually first seen in their late stages.

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:49.069
Curable in the beginning, these lesions ultimately
destroy the bone and involve the meninges

00:14:49.069 --> 00:14:50.640
and the brain.

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:57.640
Note the pulsation of the brain in this tragic
case.

00:14:57.970 --> 00:15:04.970
And now we come to the story of what can happen
to an apparently innocent mole. There are

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:11.360
few tragedies in the whole realm of medicine
that equal the complications which sometimes

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:15.850
develop in connection with these apparently
innocent lesions.

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:22.429
Since the average individual harbors about
20 moles, the malignant transformation of

00:15:22.429 --> 00:15:29.429
a mole is comparatively rare. Traumatism plays
an important role in transforming the course

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.630
of a benign nevus.

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:38.630
Moles, which are so located as to be subjected
to repeated trauma and moles showing clinical

00:15:38.799 --> 00:15:45.480
signs of activity should be treated by careful
and complete surgical removal.

00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:51.760
You have just seen a fleshy, pedunculated
mole, a type which is removed without danger.

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:56.970
The hairy non-segmented mole belongs to the
same category.

00:15:56.970 --> 00:16:02.470
Pigmented macules are common and my be single
or multiple. They may be present at birth

00:16:02.470 --> 00:16:08.799
or develop later in life. The danger of melanoma
is slight. They should be removed only on

00:16:08.799 --> 00:16:11.000
the indications mentioned.

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:17.360
It is the flat bluish black or brownish black
mole that is the most dangerous of all. And

00:16:17.360 --> 00:16:23.309
here we see a remarkable example of malignant
transformation of a bluish black mole.

00:16:23.309 --> 00:16:30.309
Metastases to the regional lymph nodes are
already present. Microscopic examination of

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:37.549
a melanoma may disclose all of the cellular
features without showing the presence of pigments

00:16:37.549 --> 00:16:43.699
or the characteristic brown intracellular
pigment may form a striking feature of the

00:16:43.699 --> 00:16:48.040
microscopic picture as you see in this photo
microgram.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:54.429
Extensive metastasis to the axillary lymph
nodes has occurred in this case following

00:16:54.429 --> 00:16:58.919
excision of a pigmented mole on the left forearm.

00:16:58.919 --> 00:17:03.630
Sometimes invasion remains limited to one
or two regional lymph nodes for a long time.

00:17:03.630 --> 00:17:08.770
And it is in this group that radical dissection
has resulted in apparent cure in isolated

00:17:08.770 --> 00:17:09.689
cases.

00:17:09.689 --> 00:17:15.949
The scar on the left forearm indicates the
site of excision of the primary melanoma.

00:17:15.949 --> 00:17:20.740
Melanoma may affect the scalp and metastasize
to regional lymph nodes as in this case.

00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:26.860
Metastasis to axillary and supraclavicular
glands also occurred in this case following

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:33.010
traumatic treatment of a mole on the left
arm. Electrodessication is uncertain and probably

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:34.500
dangerous.

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:40.750
Careful and complete surgical excision offers
the safest course. The presence of small secondary

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:46.230
nodules around a melanotic tumor is an important
sign of its malignant nature.

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:52.110
The heel is a favorite site for melanomas.
This lesion was already accompanied by pulmonary

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:55.540
metastasis when first examined.

00:17:55.540 --> 00:18:01.250
In discussing early diagnosis it is necessary
to review the steps to which a lesion passes

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:06.799
before it becomes malignant. In other words,
we must attempt to form a mental picture of

00:18:06.799 --> 00:18:09.130
the nature of the cancer process.

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:15.240
We are now fairly certain that cancer is not
a sudden event or an accident in a previously

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:21.450
normal tissue, but on the contrary it is the
result of a series of changes, which may have

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:23.360
begun many years before.

00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:29.960
A combination of factors seems necessary for
the initiation of abnormal growth. Hereditary

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:36.370
susceptibility unquestionably plays a part,
an excess or deficiency of certain hormones

00:18:36.370 --> 00:18:42.830
and probably the presence of certain chemicals
we call carcinogenic agents combined to initiate

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:45.519
excessive growth of cells.

00:18:45.519 --> 00:18:51.130
We have learned the remarkable fact that abnormal
cell growth need not necessarily result in

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:57.450
clinical cancer. At one extreme the growth
may be so rapid as to overwhelm the individual

00:18:57.450 --> 00:19:00.289
in a short period of a few months.

00:19:00.289 --> 00:19:04.639
And at the other extreme the growth may be
so slow that the patient does not live long

00:19:04.639 --> 00:19:11.380
enough to develop clinical cancer and he dies
of other causes, harboring one or more precancerous

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:12.380
lesions.

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:19.380
Thus certain precancerous lesions require
10 years, others 20 years, still others 30

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:25.340
years to reach the stage of clinical cancer.
And it is well known that the older we get

00:19:25.340 --> 00:19:29.019
the more chances we have of developing this
disease.

00:19:29.019 --> 00:19:34.659
There is also considerable evidence to indicate
that precancerous lesions can regress and

00:19:34.659 --> 00:19:40.429
perish in the body as a result of some defensive
mechanism, the nature of which we do not yet

00:19:40.429 --> 00:19:41.490
understand.

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:47.289
And it is probable that even fully established
cancers can under certain conditions cease

00:19:47.289 --> 00:19:51.279
to grow, regress, and even disappear.

00:19:51.279 --> 00:19:57.669
When we use the term precancerous we generally
think of it in microscopic terms. We mean

00:19:57.669 --> 00:20:03.570
a lesion which exhibits all the morphological
features of cancer, but which has not yet

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:06.299
escaped outside normal boundaries.

00:20:06.299 --> 00:20:11.350
We must remember, however, that the morphological
appearance of a cell is a very crude index

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:17.250
of its biological state and even a less accurate
guide as to its future intentions.

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:23.330
Thus the group of neoplastic epithelial cells
confined within the normal boundaries of the

00:20:23.330 --> 00:20:28.960
duct of the breast may be ready to invade
the lymphatics and blood vessels immediately,

00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:34.380
or they may remain stationary for many years
or they may regress and disappear.

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:39.860
And yet, the microscope, as a rule, can neither
distinguish these cells nor predict their

00:20:39.860 --> 00:20:46.860
future. Thus it is evident that cancer is
a highly complex clinical, pathological and

00:20:47.659 --> 00:20:51.200
biological problem.

00:20:51.200 --> 00:20:54.980
Through the medical and hospital service the
Veteran's Administration has developed over

00:20:54.980 --> 00:21:00.049
the past 10 years an organization for the
study and treatment of cancer that is unique

00:21:00.049 --> 00:21:01.759
in the world.

00:21:01.759 --> 00:21:06.779
In addition to the Hines Tumor Clinic, there
are five subsidiary units in the five geographical

00:21:06.779 --> 00:21:12.210
areas into which the country is divided, each
representing a unit organized, equipped, and

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:16.679
manned to offer to the veterans suffering
with cancer the latest knowledge in diagnosis

00:21:16.679 --> 00:21:18.970
and treatment of this disease.

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:24.019
An elaborate system of records is maintained
and a register of tumor cases has been established,

00:21:24.019 --> 00:21:26.889
which permits a study of resultant treatment.

00:21:26.889 --> 00:21:33.019
In addition to highly trained full-time personnel,
all six units have consulting staff composed

00:21:33.019 --> 00:21:37.940
of some of the leading experts in their field
whose help and advice are available when special

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:39.730
problems arise.

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:44.169
The Hines facility is not only a hospital
but is a practical governmentally controlled

00:21:44.169 --> 00:21:50.899
training school as well. For doctors, it presents
a broad opportunity to study diseases, inviting

00:21:50.899 --> 00:21:53.100
new methods of eliminating suffering.

00:21:53.100 --> 00:21:58.779
For patients, the library facilities and the
many phases of properly supervised occupational

00:21:58.779 --> 00:22:05.629
therapy such as wood carving, weaving, metal
work, recreation, etc. offer a greater incentive

00:22:05.629 --> 00:22:08.690
to develop new channels of thinking.

00:22:08.690 --> 00:22:13.309
Today this great facility at Hines is considered
the largest government hospital of the Veteran's

00:22:13.309 --> 00:22:18.649
Administration, a monument which should continually
inspire us to strive to conquer this dread

00:22:18.649 --> 00:22:19.940
disease.

00:22:19.940 --> 00:22:25.450
It is with such institutions as this that
the helping hand of the United States government,

00:22:25.450 --> 00:22:29.419
extended through the Veteran's Administration,
practically demonstrates its appreciation

00:22:29.419 --> 00:22:31.719
of the spirit and loyalty of its veterans.

